devices.items.description:
A single device configuration block. Note: In this Jinja2 context, items are treated as flat maps for rendering, though logically they are objects. The schema below defines the keys expected in each item map if using a flat-list structure, but per instructions, we use a flat map field-name -> type. However, since `items` must be a FLAT map of field-name to type/default/desc, here is the definition for the keys within each device item if the list items were simple objects. *Correction*: The prompt asks for `items` as a FLAT map. This implies the list contains simple objects/structs defined by the keys. Let's define the keys for each device in the list.

      *Note*: The prompt says `items` is a FLAT map field-name -> {type, default, description}. This is slightly ambiguous for lists of objects. Standard interpretation: The list elements are objects. The `items` schema describes the properties of those objects. I will provide the properties as the keys of the `items` object.
